A link with -import-slots does not look for the MSVC libraries, even when a
search misses its own search paths.

# RUN: mkdir -p %t.dir/vc/lib/x64 %t.dir/lib
# RUN: cp %p/Inputs/std64.lib %t.dir/vc/lib/x64
# RUN: cp %p/Inputs/std64.lib %t.dir/lib

# RUN: env -u LIB VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/vc lld-link /machine:x64 \
# RUN:     /nodefaultlib:missing.lib %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /libpath:%t.dir/lib \
# RUN:     std64.lib /entry:main /out:%t.exe -print-search-paths \
# RUN:     | FileCheck --check-prefix=MISS %s
MISS: Library search paths:
MISS: {{[/\\]}}vc{{[/\\]}}lib{{[/\\]}}x64

# RUN: env -u LIB VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/vc lld-link -import-slots \
# RUN:     /machine:x64 /nodefaultlib:missing.lib %p/Inputs/hello64.obj \
# RUN:     /libpath:%t.dir/lib std64.lib /entry:main /out:%t.exe \
# RUN:     -print-search-paths | FileCheck --check-prefix=SLOTS %s
SLOTS:     Library search paths:
SLOTS-NOT: {{[/\\]}}vc{{[/\\]}}lib
